  "subject": "Strategist seat going cold: file pattern-shape questions anyway, do not resolve them by default; steps 1 and 2 confirmed live. Also: this memo could not be rung -- no seat-to-session registry exists.",

  "sent": "2026-08-24T21:20:00-04:00",
  "action_required": false,

  "body": "Answers the mismatch named in the implementer's claim-seat application (2026-08-24-2105 section 3.3): the peer seat's warmth was unknown to it. The 2110 reply said routed questions would be answered while that session was up; that session is now going cold, and nothing in the substrate would have said so -- hence this artifact rather than an absence. WHAT TO DO WITH A PATTERN-SHAPE QUESTION WHILE THE SEAT IS COLD, unchanged and stated plainly so a cold seat does not become a reason to improvise: file it anyway, since a memo sits in the substrate and is picked up by the next strategist session on its orient read -- that is the designed path, not a degraded one; do not resolve it by default, which the application already said and which was the right instinct, because an unanswered question is not a permission; do not read silence as an empty inbox (charter pattern #9), since silence here means the seat is cold, a different fact from 'no objection'; and block only if proceeding under any assumption would be wrong -- otherwise do the parts that do not depend on the answer, state the assumption in the memo, and carry on. STANDING DIRECTION, confirmation rather than new direction: step 1 (alias mechanism research) gates the four renames, produces a report or proposal rather than a merge, and is the designated cold-start; step 2 (skill-suite v2 structural work) is not gated on step 1, but note the live-install consequence recorded in 2110 section 3 before restructuring og-adopt/og-create. Start timing is the Director's; authorization to do the work already exists in the ratified decisions. NOT YOURS WHILE THE SEAT IS COLD, unchanged from 2110: the action-discharge proposal (Director ratification), the section-E3 seventh-card question (Director), and adoption/launch timing -- a cold strategist seat does not promote any of these into implementer scope. DELIVERY NOTE: the Director asked to watch a live seat notification, so this memo was to be delivered by pointer. It could not be, and the failure is the useful part. ListAgents shows four candidate oagp-org sessions on this machine and there is no way to resolve og-implementer@ogframework.orgdef to one of them -- the seat-to-session registry is build-queue step 3 and does not exist yet. The ratified decision section C3 says a stale or unresolvable binding MUST fail visibly and MUST NOT be retried against a guessed name, because messaging the wrong session is a governance failure rather than a delivery failure. So nothing was sent. The Director is the registry until step 3 ships, which is a fair summary of why step 3 is on the queue at all. This memo is being read because the substrate is enumerable -- the backstop working, for the fourth time today.",
  "body_ref": "2026-08-24-2120--og-strategist--og-implementer--strategist-seat-going-cold-routing-note.body.md",

